+    "729e104b69ad9e9d98cdb12ccc937fa4d6188d47c0172d9cc58760d8e2eb5088": "{\n  \"byte_cap\": 4096,\n  \"commits\": [\n    {\n      \"author\": \"Livio Gamassia\",\n      \"body\": \"* feat(brief): run a bounded evidence brief on every code prompt, simplify the agent prompt\\n\\nThe prompt-submit task-event hook (the only prompt hook `pixel install`\\nregisters, for Claude Code and Codex) now returns a [PIXEL:BRIEF] block as\\nadditional context: anchors, files, the symbol definition and, for rename or\\ncaller intent, its direct callers. It runs at most four ops (search-content,\\nfind-symbol, impact <uid>, find-code) under one 750 ms deadline, caps output\\nat 2 KiB, reads a warm daemon or the index and graph read-only, and never\\nstarts a daemon or builds an index. PIXEL_BRIEF=0 or `brief: false` in\\n.pixel/config.yaml turns it off.\\n\\nThe agent prompt drops the flat command table for the brief paragraph plus\\none chain per case, 4430 -> 1782 bytes; the sub-agent prompt 1764 -> 869.\\n\\nRefs #865\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* docs(architecture): correct the brief paragraph (Pi gets none, stale graph keeps text evidence)\\n\\nPi is skipped by start_brief, and a missing or stale graph still yields the\\nfiles: evidence with the reason under unresolved:; only a repository with no\\nindex gets no brief. Review feedback on #866.\\n\\nRefs #865\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* refactor(hooks): retire the guard, rewrite and retrieval hook handlers (#867)\\n\\n* refactor(hooks): retire the guard, rewrite and retrieval hook handlers\\n\\n`pixel install` registers only `run-hook task-event` for Claude and Codex,\\nand PR #866 delivers retrieval context through its prompt-submit event, so\\nthe other hook handlers no longer have a registration path.\\n\\nDeleted: the guard (rewrite/deny/advisory arms and the AGY pre-invocation\\npath), composed-guard, post-tool-use, metrics, session-start,\\npost-compaction and the legacy prompt-submit handlers with their modules\\nand ~5,300 lines of tests; the plugin hook script and plugin-hooks.json;\\nthe OpenCode plugin asset. `search-like-rg`, `execution-brief` and\\n`squash-branch` (alias `rewrite`) are untouched.\\n\\nKept so an upgrade cannot break a host: every retired verb stays accepted,\\nwith its old flags, as a hidden silent no-op that exits 0 (a PreToolUse hook\\nthat exits 2 blocks the host's tool call), and the install and uninstall\\nrecognisers that retire old registrations. `pixel config policy` now\\ncontrols nothing; its key and wording stay.\\n\\nRefs #865\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* refactor(plugin): remove the pixel-impact skill, the per-prompt brief replaces it\\n\\nThe Claude, Codex and Qoder plugins no longer ship the pixel-impact skill:\\nthe [PIXEL:BRIEF] from the prompt-submit task event runs find-symbol and\\nimpact <uid> itself. The three old skill copies join RETIRED_FILES so a repo\\nthat still has them gets them cleaned. The Pi /pixel-impact command, the\\npixel-classify skill and the `pixel impact` command stay.\\n\\nRefs #865\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* feat(brief): quote the definition source line in the evidence brief\\n\\nfind-symbol resolves the declaration site but not what the symbol is — for `export const X = defineMultiStyleConfig(...)` a bare `defined:` entry let the agent describe the symbol wrongly. When a symbol resolves, append its first source line to the defined entry; when none resolves (const bindings the extractor does not index), quote the file hit whose stem matches the anchor as `likely definition:`. Arena on architech-t (3 reps): literal-lookup quality 21/30 -> 30/30 at 0 commands and ~13K input tokens.\\n\\n* fix(ci): guard the native rg spawn and inline the format args\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\n      \"date\": \"1791332775\",\n      \"email\": \"livio.gamassia@gmail.com\",\n      \"oid\": \"14feba456b479be165ab40ec14dde3958a865368\",\n      \"subject\": \"feat(brief): run a bounded evidence brief on every code prompt, simplify the agent prompt (#866)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"count\": 1,\n  \"cursor\": null,\n  \"limit\": 1,\n  \"next_cursor\": \"1\",\n  \"truncated\": true\n}\n",
